text:
Pesticides can be categorized according to their mode of action or method of application. The majority of pesticides exert their effect by intoxicating target organisms. A systemic pesticide permeates a plant after being absorbed, typically traveling upwards (via the xylem) and spreading outwards. Enhanced efficacy is often observed with systemic insecticides that contaminate flower pollen and nectar, potentially eradicating essential pollinators such as bees. [
